  ],
  "least_laxity_estimate": "deadline = submit + slack_mult x REQUESTED walltime, slack_mult=10; the ordering rule never sees true runtime",
  "secondary_on_subset": "ta_over_req_limit_pct, turnaround past the job's own declared limit, reported with n_with_req_limit because it is defined on a subset only",
  "why_not_the_plan_formula": "The submission plan sets D_i = a_i + alpha x W_i^req. On this trace that deadline is undefined or vacuous: 9000 of 13281 scored jobs (68%) declare NO walltime, 14.8% request 10 days or more, and the declared limit's p90 is 21 days against a 24-hour window. A deadline built from it fires for almost no job and not at all for two thirds of them. sla_k is defined for every job, is the metric every prior experiment in the log used, and is what the paper reports; the declared-limit metric stays as the secondary, on the 32% subset where it exists."
 },
